Fix GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq (CVE-2020-7660): sanitize RegExp.flags and validate
Date.prototype.toISOString() output before embedding them into the serialized
JavaScript string. An attacker able to supply an object whose `flags` getter or
`toISOString()` method returns attacker-controlled text (e.g. via a spoofed
object passing `instanceof RegExp`/`instanceof Date`) could break out of the
string literal and inject arbitrary code that runs when the output is eval'd.

